.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 951 AM PST Wed Nov 4 2026

Any fog or stratus from the overnight hours will continue to
dissipate over the next couple of hours. Then VFR conditions will
prevail with weak offshore flow becoming onshore with perhaps some
gusts to 15 to 25 kt at times. High clouds look to move in later
this afternoon and into the evening hours, which may linger to the
overnight. Light offshore flow or variable winds are expected as
well.

Vicinity of SFO...Offshore winds should prevail for a couple of
hours this morning with onshore winds returning by the afternoon.
Winds should increase to around 10-15kt and bring gusts up to 20-
22kt through the early evening. Winds decrease and become light and
offshore overnight. VFR conditions  expected.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Weak offshore flow will become onshore this
afternoon, with high clouds moving late this afternoon and evening.
Later tonight, light offshore flow returns while VFR conditions
prevail.

