.BEACHES...
Issued at 329 AM PST Wed Nov 4 2026

Hazardous beach conditions will be present at Pacific Coast beaches
Thursday through Saturday as long period (14-18 second)
westerly/northwesterly swell will bring an increased risk for
sneaker waves and strong rip currents with breaking waves of 12 to
16 feet. Waves can sweep across the shoreline without warning,
pulling people into the sea from beaches, jetties, and rocks. Stay
off of jetties, piers, rocks, and other waterside infrastructure.
Remain out of the water to avoid hazardous surf and never turn your
back on the ocean! Hazardous beach conditions may linger into Sunday
and Monday and thus may warrant an extension of the Beach Hazards
Statement.

